{"resourceIdentifier":"1919","resourceName":"Adeco Agropecuaria S.A. Biogas Energy Generation from Dairy Production","description":"The Project is a methane recovery through controlled anaerobic digestion and grid connected renewable electricity generation project that takes place in “Carmen” farm, located in Christophersen community, General López Department, Province of Santa Fe, Argentina.  Carmen farm has a total area of 10,042 ha dedicated to agriculture and dairy activity that consists of 2 Freestall dairy stables (FS1 and FS2) with state-of-the-art technology and a total capacity of 6,500 dairy cows.   The project consists in three mesophilic reactors that co-digest the solid organic matter (manure) from FS1 and the effluent (solid + liquid) from FS2 together with minor amounts of remains of cows’ food (corn silage, straw and other food remains) and capture the biogas produced to feed an electricity generation system of 1.4 MW that dispatches the electricity to the Argentine Interconnection System (SADI).","location":{"latitude":-34.236944,"longitude":-62.048056},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1919"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Santa Fe"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Adeco Agropecuaria S.A."},{"type":"string","value":"Buenos Aires, Argentina"},{"type":"string","value":"(+5411) 4836 8600"},{"type":"string","value":"alopez@adecoagro.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"17405"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AMS-I.D.,AMS-III.D.,AMS-III.H."}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[